WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.109
Welcome to Art-Integrated GenAI Literacy.

2
00:00:04.109 --> 00:00:08.719
GENAI 101 - Module 0: Welcome and Orientation.

3
00:00:08.719 --> 00:00:14.732
Presented by Idowu David Awoyemi, The University of Alabama.

4
00:00:15.332 --> 00:00:15.931
Welcome.

5
00:00:15.931 --> 00:00:19.224
I'm David Awoyemi, and I'm glad you're here.

6
00:00:19.224 --> 00:00:29.928
This course exists because the students you will teach are
growing up in a world where generative AI is part of how
music and theater get made.

7
00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:38.386
Your ability to navigate these tools, and to guide your
students in using them well, will shape what they create.

8
00:00:38.386 --> 00:00:44.299
We're going to build that ability the way artists learn
best: by making things.

9
00:00:44.299 --> 00:00:53.506
Over the next few weeks you'll compose, produce, score,
write, direct, and choreograph with AI tools as your
collaborators.

10
00:00:54.106 --> 00:00:56.629
Here is the shape of the course.

11
00:00:56.629 --> 00:01:05.068
Module zero is orientation: you'll set up free accounts,
meet your peers, and take a short self-assessment.

12
00:01:05.068 --> 00:01:08.853
Module one is music, with four hands-on lessons.

13
00:01:08.853 --> 00:01:12.481
Module two is theater, also with four lessons.

14
00:01:12.481 --> 00:01:20.289
You can take those two modules in either order, so start
with the one closest to your own teaching.

15
00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:27.781
Module three asks you to turn one of your projects into a
lesson plan for your future students.

16
00:01:27.781 --> 00:01:32.434
Plan on twelve to sixteen hours in total, at your own pace.

17
00:01:33.034 --> 00:01:38.497
Every lesson follows the same rhythm, so you always know
what comes next.

18
00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:43.137
You watch a short video like this one and read the
objectives.

19
00:01:43.137 --> 00:01:48.973
You learn the key ideas behind the tool and the competency
the lesson targets.

20
00:01:48.973 --> 00:01:51.293
You do a step-by-step activity.

21
00:01:51.293 --> 00:01:57.953
You create a shareable artifact: a song, a beat, a scored
scene, a script, a performance.

22
00:01:57.953 --> 00:02:04.464
You share it in the lesson gallery with a rationale of no
more than seventy-five words.

23
00:02:04.464 --> 00:02:11.573
Then you check your understanding with a short quiz and
answer two or three reflection prompts.

24
00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:26.764
Underneath the projects are seven competencies:
computational thinking, prompt engineering, problem solving,
creativity and innovation, AI feedback evaluation, AI ethics
literacy, and collaboration.

25
00:02:26.764 --> 00:02:34.723
Each lesson targets two or three of them, and every artifact
you make is evidence of growth in at least one.

26
00:02:34.723 --> 00:02:42.388
You'll rate yourself on all seven at the start and again at
the end, so you can see how far you've come.

27
00:02:42.988 --> 00:02:47.445
Assessment is competency-based, and there are no timed
exams.

28
00:02:47.445 --> 00:02:55.410
The eight gallery posts count for forty percent and are
marked complete or incomplete, with feedback from me.

29
00:02:55.410 --> 00:03:01.914
The knowledge checks count for ten percent, and you can
retake them as often as you like.

30
00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:05.713
The two module reflections count for twenty percent.

31
00:03:05.713 --> 00:03:12.290
The final project, your lesson plan, counts for thirty
percent and includes peer feedback.

32
00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.601
Eighty percent or higher earns a certificate of completion.

33
00:03:17.201 --> 00:03:19.627
Three things before you begin.

34
00:03:19.627 --> 00:03:27.551
First, set up the free accounts listed on the tools page so
the lessons flow without interruption.

35
00:03:27.551 --> 00:03:31.270
Second, read the page on using AI responsibly.

36
00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:40.326
The short version: disclose when you use AI, credit the
tool, and never clone a real person's voice or likeness.

37
00:03:40.326 --> 00:03:51.484
Third, introduce yourself in the forum, and post any course
questions in the pinned Questions thread so everyone
benefits from the answer.

38
00:03:51.484 --> 00:03:52.535
Let's create.

39
00:03:52.535 --> 00:03:53.747
Let's innovate.

40
00:03:53.747 --> 00:03:54.637
Let's lead.

41
00:03:54.637 --> 00:03:56.820
I'll see you in Module one.
